---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="Under the hood" description="How Thought Control is built: an append-only event log, a pure replay, one primitive, and caretline, the editor engine with exact caret motion." tab="hood">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker"><span class="blk" aria-hidden="true"></span>under the hood</p>
    <h1>How it's built</h1>
    <p class="lede">One Rust binary. An append-only log as the truth, a database you can delete, and an editor engine with a test for every rule about where the caret goes. Here are the highlights; the <a href={u('docs/architecture/')}>architecture docs</a> go all the way down.</p>
  </header>

  <figure class="arch">
    <svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 760 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="a-t">
      <title id="a-t">The CLI, TUI and daemon share one core. Ops become events in a per-device log; replay builds a SQLite store; queries and views read it.</title>
      <defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M1 1L9 5L1 9" /></marker></defs>
      <rect x="16" y="20" width="132" height="44" rx="3" /><text x="32" y="47" class="t">thc (CLI)</text>
      <rect x="16" y="80" width="132" height="44" rx="3" /><text x="32" y="107" class="t">thc tui</text>
      <rect x="16" y="140" width="132" height="44" rx="3" /><text x="32" y="167" class="t">◆ agents</text>
      <path d="M148 42 C 190 42, 190 96, 226 100" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M148 102 H 226" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M148 162 C 190 162, 190 108, 226 104" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <text x="168" y="92">ops</text>
      <rect x="230" y="78" width="130" height="50" rx="3" /><text x="246" y="100" class="t">one writer</text><text x="246" y="118">per device</text>
      <path d="M360 103 H 406" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <rect x="410" y="60" width="150" height="86" rx="3" class="e" /><text x="426" y="84" class="t">log/&lt;device&gt;/</text><text x="426" y="104">*.jsonl</text><text x="426" y="124" class="e">append-only</text>
      <path d="M485 146 V 196" marker-end="url(#ah)" /><text x="494" y="178">replay (pure)</text>
      <rect x="410" y="200" width="150" height="50" rx="3" stroke-dasharray="3 4" /><text x="426" y="222" class="t">SQLite store</text><text x="426" y="240">a cache</text>
      <path d="M560 225 H 606" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <rect x="610" y="200" width="134" height="50" rx="3" /><text x="626" y="222" class="t">queries</text><text x="626" y="240">views · @today</text>
      <path d="M677 200 V 40 H 152" stroke-dasharray="2 4" marker-end="url(#ah)" /><text x="420" y="32">reads, and live updates from the daemon</text>
      <text x="16" y="285" class="dim">the vault folder holds only the log (synced); the store is local and rebuildable</text>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <div class="grid">
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="history" /><h3>An append-only log</h3><p>Every change is one JSON line in this device's own file. Sync tools never see two writers on one file, so there are no conflicted copies.</p></div>
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="clock" /><h3>A pure replay</h3><p>State is a function of the events: clocks, randomness and timezones live only in the writer. Delete the database and <code>thc rebuild</code> replays it.</p></div>
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="sync" /><h3>Merges that converge</h3><p>A hybrid logical clock orders events across devices. The newest field wins; concurrent text edits keep both versions for you to choose.</p></div>
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="vault" /><h3>One primitive</h3><p>A page, a day, a task and a tag are all nodes. "Task" is a status, "reminder" is an alert: fewer kinds, fewer edge cases.</p></div>
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="pen" /><h3>caretline, the editor</h3><p>The editor engine, now its own Rust crate (<a href="https://caretline.app">caretline.app</a>, <code>cargo add caretline</code>): a plain-text block editor with documents and views, Markdown in and out, and one layout map for drawing, clicks and motion. Every caret position belongs to exactly one row. It comes with a small example: a whole Markdown editor in the terminal, in about 160 lines on top of the engine.</p></div>
    <div class="cell"><Icon name="bug" /><h3>Rules that run</h3><p>Caret motion is pure functions with invariants, checked over random documents, with golden examples written in a caret notation that reads like the docs.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">a caret example</div>
  <pre class="fx"><code>{`width 40
---
The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog and keeps running through the long `}<span class="accent">▮</span>{`grass until dusk.

Short one.
---
↓   Short one.  at `}<span class="accent">▮</span>{`Short`}</code></pre>
  <p class="muted">A golden test, as written: the caret at the start of a wrapped row, one <kbd>↓</kbd>, and where it must land. caretline runs 103 of these (22 for motion, 81 for editing), plus property tests over random documents: a motion without <kbd>⇧</kbd> never leaves a selection, cut then paste changes nothing, and changing a line into a task never moves another line.</p>

  <p class="next">The full story, module by module and decision by decision, is in the <a href={u('docs/architecture/')}>architecture docs</a>. caretline has <a href="https://caretline.app">its own site</a>, with docs and a playground. Meanwhile, the <a href={u('docs/philosophy/')}>philosophy</a> explains the why, and the <a href={u('landscape/')}>landscape</a> maps the tools nearby, what we'd only be reinventing, and the gap we're building for.</p>
</Base>
<style>
  .arch { margin: 0 0 3rem; }
  .arch svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .art text.dim { fill: var(--dim); }
  .fx { font-size: 13px; }
  .next { margin-top: 3rem; }
</style>
